# member = handedIn[someName]; handedIn.has(1)
# The read under a key nobody knows hands out every member, and all of them are held. `x.has(..)` on an object nobody knows calls what the read of `has` has answered:
# of the built-ins that have escaped a member under that name, and no other. Beside the unknown object the callees do not list what has escaped, so the call applies those members itself.
# RUN: valueflow-solve used
# CHECK-NOT: run MapPrototypeGet
# CHECK: used MapPrototypeGet
# CHECK: run MapPrototypeHas

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="handedIn" [isFreeName]
    v2 = PropGet v0 key="someName" [isFreeName]
    v3 = ElemGet v1, v2
    v4 = PropGet v1 key="has"
    v5 = Integer integer=1
    v6 = Call v4, v1, v5 calleeKey="has"
    Return
}
